From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:56:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 26/51] =?UTF-8?q?objects:=20paper=20=C2=A74=20variable-siz?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20objects=20with=20create/read=5Fstart/read=5Fend/write=5Fsta?=
 =?UTF-8?q?rt/write=5Fend?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ObjectCreate(id, size) bump-allocates contiguous bytes in an SWcc arena (64 B or
4 KiB aligned, no free) and publishes the descriptor (location, size) in the
object's own index entry through the NR log. One object = one entry = one
coherence record: none at create in the megalon flavor (paper §3.4.2), a static
record per object in hwcc. Sections run the slot path's own functions
(GetAnchor, read_seq_start/end, write_seq_start/end, SwitchRW, reclaim, replay)
with the slot range replaced by the object's [ptr, ptr+size); data is read and
written in place. Slot Put/Get paths are unchanged. Config keys
object_arena_size (0 = disabled, layout unchanged), object_align,
object_max_count. Test binary object-test (2 nodes, self-checking).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
